{"kind":"artifact","text":"notes/2026-10-01-jam-room.md at exact 798ac2a300b19405174d4a23f6747ed619da7ef0 on request/jam-room-r6, under promise git:sha1…5219771 on request git:sha1…3969c35\n\nJam room, revision 7 at 798ac2a300b19405174d4a23f6747ed619da7ef0 on request/jam-room-r6, for request 9ce8533f, answering the checker's changes-requested verdict 696f25ec on b188c7f3. Subject: notes/2026-10-01-jam-room.md. Design only; nothing was run. It is a prose integration of the planner's decisions dff56797, with no new design. A pattern has one derived start bar: it may state its length and the interpretation it follows and never its start bar; the bar is computed from the entry's time, the lookahead in force for that entry and the tempo schedule of lower sequence. A sing records a kind, tune or rhythm; the rhythm phrase is a second sing, and its interpretation sets tempo and grid and keeps the tune's key. The lookahead is a value of the jam definition's rules item, set at founding and changed by a rules act; the definition stays immutable; each pattern uses the lookahead in force for its own entry. A refused act writes no entry: the caller receives the refusal and the stage shows it, which is display and not the room's history; a durable trace of refusals would be separate platform work. Three clarifications from the verdict are made: spike J2 reports the actual interval from the end of a phrase to the band's first downbeat beside its target and the human judgment; a dated line says the third I3 milestone landed as f47fc598 on 2026-10-06, where a founding still stops at the destination's creation; and the entry-rate figures are ceilings from one temporary budget that exclude other entries. Two questions stay open as revision 6 wrote them (whether a solo's notes are recorded, and the transport origin), since the planner's act says the other resolutions stand as written. The questions for the owner stand: listening to the comparison files, five phrases by two people, whether a hosted audio model may be called, how long a gap is still funny, and whether any of the person's audio is kept. The author checked by search that no sentence still offers a chosen bar, an open rhythm-phrase question, an unplaced lookahead or a recorded refusal.","body":{"commit":"798ac2a300b19405174d4a23f6747ed619da7ef0","path":"notes/2026-10-01-jam-room.md"}}